  "articleSummary": "**Summary:**\n\n* **Core Thesis:** The primary security threat of AI agents is not a single sci-fi breakthrough, but the compounding multiplication of agent endurance (task duration) and breadth (orchestrated sub-agents), amplified by \"LLMjacking\" where attackers use stolen credentials to run attacks on the victim's dime. \n* **Key Technologies & Concepts:** METR time-horizon benchmarks for agent task length, multi-agent orchestration frameworks (referenced via Anthropic's Claude Code / GTG-1002 espionage incident), and cloud security vulnerabilities (Sysdig's LLMjacking). \n* **Tone & Framing:** Written as a pragmatic, slightly cynical technical analysis / warning to engineering teams, framed heavily through the pop-culture metaphor of *The Terminator* (\"absolutely will not stop... billing\"). \n* **Intended Audience:** Software engineering teams, security professionals, and AI practitioners who downplay the agentic threat as hype.",
